{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_c877b00ca0134973a2d097da","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse harness\n2\t\n3\t# Slice: readme.quickstart install-root isolation (Canary 9 exact red, #1881 / #863 gate 3)\n4\t\n5\t## SKILL\n6\t\n7\tLoad and follow: `.agents/skills/netscript-harness`, `.agents/skills/netscript-doctrine`,\n8\t`.agents/skills/netscript-tools`, `.agents/skills/netscript-pr`, `.agents/skills/aspire`.\n9\tArchetype 6 (CLI/tooling), nested E2E gate workspace `packages/cli/e2e`. Gate code only — no\n10\tproduct behaviour, no `packages/*/src` outside `packages/cli/e2e`, no `plugins/`, no lockfile.\n11\t\n12\t## Exact red (immutable evidence, do not rerun)\n13\t\n14\tCanary 9 `e2e-cli-prod` run 33704697088 at `v0.0.7-canary.9`: scaffold.runtime and\n15\tquickstart.walk PASSED; `readme.quickstart.01-install-cli` FAILED, exit 1, receipt 01.json:\n16\targv `deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli@0.0.7-canary.9`,\n17\tstderr `error: Existing installation found. Aborting (Use -f to overwrite).`. Cause: the workflow's\n18\tearlier \"Install published CLI from JSR\" step already owns the ambient global `netscript`; the\n19\tREADME command inherits the runner env (`runCommand` → `runAspireCommand` in\n20\t`packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/quickstart/readme-command.ts` passes no `env`).\n21\t`cleanup.aspire-stop` red is downstream (scaffold never ran) — do not touch cleanup.\n22\t\n23\t## Fix (decided; no owner decision)\n24\t\n25\t1. In `readme-command.ts`: derive a run-owned install root `resolve(runRoot, '.deno-install')`\n26\t   (created on index 0 in `initializeState`, recorded in `ReadmeWalkState` as\n27\t   `denoInstallRoot`). Spawn EVERY README command (all indexes, not just index 0) with env\n28\t   `DENO_INSTALL_ROOT=<root>` and `PATH=<root>/bin<delimiter><ambient PATH>` so command 1\n29\t   installs into the isolated root and later `netscript …` commands resolve to exactly the binary\n30\t   the README installed. `aspire`, `deno`, `curl` still resolve from the ambient PATH tail.\n31\t2. Extend `runAspireCommand(command, cwd, timeoutMs, env?)` in `aspire-walk.ts` with an optional\n32\t   `env: Record<string,string>` (merged over inherited env via `Deno.Command({ env })`). Default\n33\t   behaviour for `quickstart.walk` MUST be unchanged (no env passed there).\n34\t3. Receipt: add `environment: { denoInstallRoot, pathPrepend }` to `ReadmeCommandReceipt` so the\n35\t   hosted receipt proves isolation. argv stays verbatim — NEVER add `-f`, never edit README.md,\n36\t   never uninstall/remove the workflow's prior install, no retry, no fallback.\n37\t4. Do NOT change `.github/workflows/e2e-cli-prod.yml`.\n38\t\n39\t## RED/GREEN proof (required)\n40\t\n41\t- RED first: a focused test in `packages/cli/e2e/tests/presentation/readme-quickstart-suite_test.ts`\n42\t  (or a new `tests/application/readme-command_test.ts`) that drives index 0 through the command\n43\t  seam with a fake runner/recorded spawn and asserts (a) the spawned env carries\n44\t  `DENO_INSTALL_ROOT` under `runRoot` and `PATH` starting with `<root>/bin`, (b) argv is byte-\n45\t  identical to the README command with only `<version>` substituted (no `-f`), (c) index ≥1\n46\t  commands carry the same env. Commit the failing test, then the fix, then the green run — cite\n47\t  both outputs in the worklog. If a spawn seam does not exist, add the smallest injectable\n48\t  `spawn` parameter (default = real) — no test-only branches in production paths.\n49\t- Existing tests must stay green: `readme-quickstart_test.ts`, drift test, suite/registry tests.\n50\t\n51\t## Gates (scoped; no runtime)\n52\t\n53\t`deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-check.ts --root packages/cli/e2e --ext ts,tsx`;\n54\t`deno run --allow-read --allow-write --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-test.ts -- --allow-all packages/cli/e2e/tests`;\n55\t`deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-fmt.ts --root packages/cli/e2e --ext ts,tsx`;\n56\tlint on changed files only (desktop-native fixture `catalog:` refusal is a known baseline);\n57\t`deno task e2e:cli gates readme.quickstart` (listing only). Do NOT run readme.quickstart,\n58\tquickstart.walk, scaffold runtime suites, Aspire, or Docker.\n59\t\n60\t## PR\n61\t\n62\tBranch `fix/aspire-1881-readme-install-isolation` off main `45e57377f`. Title:\n63\t\"fix(e2e): isolate DENO_INSTALL_ROOT for the verbatim README quickstart walk (#863 gate 3)\".\n64\tBody: exact red above with run id and stderr line; RED/GREEN outputs; `Part of #1881` and\n65\t`Part of #863` (NO closing keyword — #1881 closes only on the green hosted transcript). Labels\n66\t`type:fix area:cli area:aspire gate:e2e priority:p0 orchestrator:aspire status:impl`, milestone\n67\t0.0.7. Open non-draft. Record worklog/drift under\n68\t`.llm/runs/research-aspire-13.5-adoption--0.0.7/slices/leaf-1881-fix/`. Do not mark ready-merge.\n69\t\n70\t## Addendum (coordinator, required)\n71\t\n72\t- `initializeState` at index 0 MUST remove any pre-existing `<runRoot>/.deno-install` (recursive,\n73\t  NotFound tolerated) before recreating it — `mkdir recursive` alone leaves a prior `netscript` and\n74\t  reproduces the collision on rerun. Later indexes inherit the persisted root/PATH from state.\n75\t- The RED/GREEN test must seed a fake `<runRoot>/.deno-install/bin/netscript` before index 0 and\n76\t  prove it is gone after `initializeState`, while argv stays verbatim and index ≥1 carries the\n77\t  same env. Keep scope bounded; nothing else changes.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"229add02-ca41-444b-82ba-387aaf5372ff","uuid":"b9e18fa8-3401-4c57-a040-03f8006bac39","timestamp":"2026-09-03T02:20:42.214Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/projects/netscript/worktrees/007-aspire/.llm/runs/research-aspire-13.5-adoption--0.0.7/slices/leaf-1881-fix/brief.md","content":"use harness\n\n# Slice: readme.quickstart install-root isolation (Canary 9 exact red, #1881 / #863 gate 3)\n\n## SKILL\n\nLoad and follow: `.agents/skills/netscript-harness`, `.agents/skills/netscript-doctrine`,\n`.agents/skills/netscript-tools`, `.agents/skills/netscript-pr`, `.agents/skills/aspire`.\nArchetype 6 (CLI/tooling), nested E2E gate workspace `packages/cli/e2e`. Gate code only — no\nproduct behaviour, no `packages/*/src` outside `packages/cli/e2e`, no `plugins/`, no lockfile.\n\n## Exact red (immutable evidence, do not rerun)\n\nCanary 9 `e2e-cli-prod` run 33704697088 at `v0.0.7-canary.9`: scaffold.runtime and\nquickstart.walk PASSED; `readme.quickstart.01-install-cli` FAILED, exit 1, receipt 01.json:\nargv `deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli@0.0.7-canary.9`,\nstderr `error: Existing installation found. Aborting (Use -f to overwrite).`. Cause: the workflow's\nearlier \"Install published CLI from JSR\" step already owns the ambient global `netscript`; the\nREADME command inherits the runner env (`runCommand` → `runAspireCommand` in\n`packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/quickstart/readme-command.ts` passes no `env`).\n`cleanup.aspire-stop` red is downstream (scaffold never ran) — do not touch cleanup.\n\n## Fix (decided; no owner decision)\n\n1. In `readme-command.ts`: derive a run-owned install root `resolve(runRoot, '.deno-install')`\n   (created on index 0 in `initializeState`, recorded in `ReadmeWalkState` as\n   `denoInstallRoot`). Spawn EVERY README command (all indexes, not just index 0) with env\n   `DENO_INSTALL_ROOT=<root>` and `PATH=<root>/bin<delimiter><ambient PATH>` so command 1\n   installs into the isolated root and later `netscript …` commands resolve to exactly the binary\n   the README installed. `aspire`, `deno`, `curl` still resolve from the ambient PATH tail.\n2. Extend `runAspireCommand(command, cwd, timeoutMs, env?)` in `aspire-walk.ts` with an optional\n   `env: Record<string,string>` (merged over inherited env via `Deno.Command({ env })`). Default\n   behaviour for `quickstart.walk` MUST be unchanged (no env passed there).\n3. Receipt: add `environment: { denoInstallRoot, pathPrepend }` to `ReadmeCommandReceipt` so the\n   hosted receipt proves isolation. argv stays verbatim — NEVER add `-f`, never edit README.md,\n   never uninstall/remove the workflow's prior install, no retry, no fallback.\n4. Do NOT change `.github/workflows/e2e-cli-prod.yml`.\n\n## RED/GREEN proof (required)\n\n- RED first: a focused test in `packages/cli/e2e/tests/presentation/readme-quickstart-suite_test.ts`\n  (or a new `tests/application/readme-command_test.ts`) that drives index 0 through the command\n  seam with a fake runner/recorded spawn and asserts (a) the spawned env carries\n  `DENO_INSTALL_ROOT` under `runRoot` and `PATH` starting with `<root>/bin`, (b) argv is byte-\n  identical to the README command with only `<version>` substituted (no `-f`), (c) index ≥1\n  commands carry the same env. Commit the failing test, then the fix, then the green run — cite\n  both outputs in the worklog. If a spawn seam does not exist, add the smallest injectable\n  `spawn` parameter (default = real) — no test-only branches in production paths.\n- Existing tests must stay green: `readme-quickstart_test.ts`, drift test, suite/registry tests.\n\n## Gates (scoped; no runtime)\n\n`deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-check.ts --root packages/cli/e2e --ext ts,tsx`;\n`deno run --allow-read --allow-write --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-test.ts -- --allow-all packages/cli/e2e/tests`;\n`deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-fmt.ts --root packages/cli/e2e --ext ts,tsx`;\nlint on changed files only (desktop-native fixture `catalog:` refusal is a known baseline);\n`deno task e2e:cli gates readme.quickstart` (listing only). Do NOT run readme.quickstart,\nquickstart.walk, scaffold runtime suites, Aspire, or Docker.\n\n## PR\n\nBranch `fix/aspire-1881-readme-install-isolation` off main `45e57377f`. Title:\n\"fix(e2e): isolate DENO_INSTALL_ROOT for the verbatim README quickstart walk (#863 gate 3)\".\nBody: exact red above with run id and stderr line; RED/GREEN outputs; `Part of #1881` and\n`Part of #863` (NO closing keyword — #1881 closes only on the green hosted transcript). Labels\n`type:fix area:cli area:aspire gate:e2e priority:p0 orchestrator:aspire status:impl`, milestone\n0.0.7. Open non-draft. Record worklog/drift under\n`.llm/runs/research-aspire-13.5-adoption--0.0.7/slices/leaf-1881-fix/`. Do not mark ready-merge.\n\n## Addendum (coordinator, required)\n\n- `initializeState` at index 0 MUST remove any pre-existing `<runRoot>/.deno-install` (recursive,\n  NotFound tolerated) before recreating it — `mkdir recursive` alone leaves a prior `netscript` and\n  reproduces the collision on rerun. Later indexes inherit the persisted root/PATH from state.\n- The RED/GREEN test must seed a fake `<runRoot>/.deno-install/bin/netscript` before index 0 and\n  prove it is gone after `initializeState`, while argv stays verbatim and index ≥1 carries the\n  same env. Keep scope bounded; nothing else changes.\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
